# Data
# Anchored to the project root on purpose: an unanchored "data/" also matches
# src/uplift/data/, which is the ingest package, not a dataset. Nothing under
# data/ is versioned, not even a .gitkeep: git does not descend into an excluded
# directory, so a "!" exception below this rule could never take effect. The
# scripts create data/raw/ and data/processed/ themselves.
/data/
*.csv
*.gz
*.parquet
*.pkl
*.joblib

# Credentials
.env
*.pem

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Run outputs. reports/data_summary.json IS versioned: the published dataset
# figures come from it. The memory probe is machine specific and stays local.
reports/peak_memory.json
reports/*.parquet
reports/*.csv
